    Inputs having ``nan``:

    >>> nan = jnp.nan
    >>> x2 = jnp.array([nan, -3, 9])
    >>> y2 = jnp.array([[4, -2, nan],
    ...                 [-3, -5, 10]])
    >>> jnp.maximum(x2, y2)
    Array([[nan, -2., nan],
          [nan, -3., 10.]], dtype=float32)

